# Git Commits

- Never add `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` or any Cursor/AI co-author trailer to commit messages.

# Pre-Push Checklist

Before every `git push`, run the TypeScript compiler across all packages and fix any errors:

```bash
# frontend
cd frontend && node_modules/.bin/tsc --noEmit

# backend
cd backend && node_modules/.bin/tsc --noEmit
```

Common pitfall — `useState` infers a **literal type** from its initial value, so the setter won't accept a broader union:

```tsx
// ❌ infers useState<'0'> — setFoo('1') is a type error
const [foo, setFoo] = useState(() => readPref(KEY, '0'));

// ✅ explicitly widen to string
const [foo, setFoo] = useState<string>(() => readPref(KEY, '0'));
```

Never push code that fails `tsc --noEmit`.
